WEBVTT

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.070
Let's see...

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.480
Hiromi!

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.110
Over here!

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.560
Good morning, Tomo-chan.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.890
Good morning. The weather's nice.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.390
Yeah.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:24.410
Then shall we get started 
on my Kamakura tour?

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.330
Yeah.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:59.970
<b>Kamakura
Bike
Rental</b>

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.430
I'm sorry.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:07.300
This is the only women's 
bike we have right now.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:07.790
<b>#2  Go Explore Kamakura!</b>

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.310
The rest are cross bikes.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.570
What do you want to do, Hiromi?

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.440
I prefer this one, since I'm used to it.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.810
So I'll be riding a cross bike, huh?

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.910
I've never ridden one of these before.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.930
I think you'll be fine 
if you can ride a bike.

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.540
Then we'll take these, please.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.660
This is your shifter.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.690
Pull on it, and you'll shift up.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.580
Push this, and you'll shift down.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.930
Good morning!

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:44.300
Sh-Shiki-sensei?

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.030
Surprised, girls?

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.400
What are you doing today?
Going cycling together?

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:56.080
Yes. Since Hiromi just moved here,
I thought I'd show her around the area.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.440
Oh, perfect.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.160
Could you show me around, too?

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:01.660
What?

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.830
I actually just moved here, too,
and don't know the area very well.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.050
I got lost while riding around.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.040
You don't mind having just 
one more person, do you?

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.820
We'd love to have you. Right, Tomo-chan?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:20.420
Of course. The more, the merrier.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.910
That's the spirit.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.220
Way to go, my students.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.000
We'll start by heading towards the ocean.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.310
Is everyone ready?

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.600
Yeah.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:33.850
Okay, then...

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.150
What's wrong?

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.610
The pedals are so heavy.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.330
Akitsuki-san, you can't 
start on such a heavy gear.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:45.910
What?

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.180
Didn't he just show you?

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.920
You want to start on a lower gear 
and shift up to match your speed.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.490
Oh, right.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.020
Tomo-chan, you can't ride a bicycle, either?

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.100
You're just like I was.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.400
I... I'm just not used to using one of these.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:09.020
But now that I take a closer look,
there are a ton of gears on a cross bike.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:14.320
There are three on the front, and on the 
back there are one, two, three, four...

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.440
Eight gears?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.360
How am I supposed to match 
this many gears to my speed?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.790
Well...

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.780
By using your instincts, of course.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.910
What?

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.370
Once you start riding, 
you'll learn soon enough.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.830
That's rather vague.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.420
Now it's totally different from earlier.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.170
Isn't it?

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.130
Yes.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.470
You're both so fast.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:57.730
Shiki-sensei, Tomo-chan, wait!

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:02.360
I missed my shot.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:07.170
Since you two aren't wearing helmets,
don't go too fast.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.120
Okay.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.410
What are they up to?

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:21.690
I came all the way here since
 I heard there were rare birds here.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.890
But you missed your shot.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.080
This isn't any fun.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:29.260
I'm sorry, Lady Fuyune.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.340
Let's go.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.930
Yes, miss.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:51.320
Sightseeing with your own two feet, huh?

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.370
Why are you stopping?

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.260
What is this?

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.630
This street gets crowded sometimes.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.490
Sheesh...

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.530
It's nice how bicycles don't 
have to deal with traffic.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:20.160
Oh, right. Those would be the same as 
traveling on your own two feet, right?

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.820
Gramps, change of plans.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.520
Head to the bicycle shop.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>Kamakura's Famous
Meoto Manju</b>

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>Chikaramochi-ya</b>

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.960
<b>Kamakura's Famous
Meoto Manju</b>

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.960
<b>Chikaramochi-ya</b>

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.680
<b>Goryo
 Shrine</b>

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.070
Delicious!

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.760
Where should we go next?

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:17.370
I recommend the Zeniarai 
Benten Shrine, but...

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.610
Sensei?

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:22.670
Oh, I'm sorry. I suddenly 
feel so sleepy after eating.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.210
She's asleep.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.520
It can't be helped.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:31.220
Let's rest for a while, too.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.740
Could I borrow your bike, then?

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.050
What?

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:39.020
I want to try riding a cross bike, too.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.340
It that okay?

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.310
Sure, but...

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.250
It's okay. I won't go that far.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:46.020
Here.

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.550
The seat's a little high.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:08:00.040
This shifter's for the front 
and this one's for the back.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.610
Now, let's go!

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:14.220
I need to shift gears to match my speed.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.830
Wow, I'm going faster.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.060
Am I really doing this?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.990
This bike is fun.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.840
How far did Hiromi go?

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.270
Shiki-sensei's still fast asleep, too.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.580
What?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:46.220
<i>Is... Is this the "apologizing 
sleeper" pose I've heard about?</i>

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:46.600
<b>Apologizing Sleeper</b>

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.310
Akitsuki-san, is something wrong?

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:54.340
No. Actually, Hiromi still 
hasn't come back yet.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.910
Why don't you call her cell phone, then?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.260
I'll try doing that.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.110
Huh?

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.530
Well, that's a problem.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.040
Where am I?

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:26.220
I started out near the shrine.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:29.080
But I saw a squirrel, so I chased after it.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.050
Then I tried to get back through an alleyway.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:37.010
When I came to a train crossing, I crossed it,
but it wasn't the one near the shrine.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:43.030
I can't remember how I got here, I don't 
know where I am, and I forgot my phone.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:47.140
Am I lost?

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:53.780
An apple?

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.260
What is this?

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.950
Oh, my. I'm sorry.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.900
My bag ripped.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:06.160
Here you go, ma'am.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.040
Thank you.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:15.040
Oh, right. Ma'am, I'm looking for a shrine.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:19.130
Um, what's the name of that shrine?

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:22.310
Is it... the Thank You Shrine?

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:23.780
Thank you?

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:27.200
Oh, right. I need to thank you.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:28.520
Here you go.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.910
What? Are you sure?

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:34.730
Yes. It's not one of the ones
 I dropped, so don't worry.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.990
Thank you, then.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:40.780
Delicious!

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:46.120
Oh, right. You said you're 
looking for a shrine, right?

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:47.470
Yes.

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:51.630
There's a shrine past the 
top of this mountain.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.840
Past the top?

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.160
Thanks, ma'am.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:58.910
Oh, but going by bike is...

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.620
I'm off.

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:02.050
Be careful.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:03.720
Okay.

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:08.810
Yes, this is Bakery Flat.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:12.190
Hey, Sis. Are you lost?

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:15.940
Actually, I'm not the one who's lost.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:20.200
Is this really the right way?

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:25.490
I see. In that case, I know 
the perfect customers.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:29.960
Sabaya-san, Alpaca-san, Tootsie-san...

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:33.170
Could you do me a favor?

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.130
Of course!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.720
Your target is this girl.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:44.770
If you find her, I'll give you some 
of my special walnut jam rolls.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:45.890
Do your best.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.720
Roger that!

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:56.830
Um, excuse me. I have a flat tire.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:58.120
Oh, sorry.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:00.570
We're not a bike shop. We're a bakery.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:01.650
What?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.850
Could you lift your front wheel for me?

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:07.990
O-Okay.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:11.780
I don't see any big holes.

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:13.750
Did your tube get caught in the rim?

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:17.350
Um, this isn't a bike shop, right?

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:18.710
Excuse me, shopkeeper.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.630
I'd like one bicycle, please.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.180
<b>Sasuke
Inari
Shrine</b>

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.640
<b>I wish to get better at drawing</b>

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.510
Oinari-sama, Oinari-sama.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:34.660
I promise to continue studying art, 
so please grant me your blessing.

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:39.520
I thought of something.

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:47.950
There.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.910
It's a priestess with cat ears.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:53.250
<b>Sasuke
Inari
Shrine</b>

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:57.160
Um, this place is a shrine, right?

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:59.960
Yes, it's the Sasuke Inari Shrine.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.710
What did you just say?

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:05.420
Sasuke Inari Shrine.

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:07.250
Sasuke?

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:11.940
I see.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.430
You were looking for a shrine.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:16.680
But I can't remember the name.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:21.000
It was something like Thank You or Sorry.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.330
Thank you... sorry...

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:25.900
Could it be...

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.840
Yes, that's it.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.900
What? You're not a bicycle shop?

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:39.520
No, we're Bakery Flat.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.590
The store next door is Cycle Flat.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:46.570
How confusing. And they're not open.

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:50.160
The owner of the bike shop is 
traveling overseas right now,

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.710
but is supposed to come back next week.

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:54.920
Okay.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:57.840
Since I switched out your tube,
you should be fine now.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:01.180
You can fix bicycles,
even though you're a baker?

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:02.980
I can manage this much.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.400
That should do it.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:11.950
Thank you. Um, how much for the tube?

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:16.000
It's fine. Cyclists help each other 
out when they're in trouble.

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:20.860
But you should at least learn 
how to fix a flat tire.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:24.120
Sorry. I just started riding.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:25.180
I see.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:30.730
What do you think is most 
important to a cyclist?

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:31.140
What?

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.890
Going fast, maybe?

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.140
Sure, if you're a professional,

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:40.980
but for ordinary people, the most 
important thing is making it home safe.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:47.730
Even if you get a flat tire, or it rains,
or you fall asleep from exhaustion,

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:52.450
as long as you make it home okay,
you can ride and enjoy your bike again.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:52.970
Right?

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:53.530
Yeah.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:59.770
And the best way to have fun and stay 
safe is to find friends to ride with you.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:02.210
Um, can I help you?

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.460
That bicycle looks fast.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.130
What? Uh, I guess.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.300
What's your name?

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.430
Higa Natsumi.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.540
I'm Kamikura Fuyune.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.730
Could you let me ride your bike?

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:17.560
What?

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:22.520
It's just a short ride to the Goryo Shrine, 
so I'll show you the way.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.200
Really?

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:28.390
Oh, good. Now I can get back to Tomo-chan.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:29.320
Tomo?

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.280
Found you.

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.280
Wh-Who are you?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.030
Get her!

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.700
What?!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:41.950
Um, please be careful.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:44.290
I'm not going to break it.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:45.670
What is this?

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:50.590
The handlebar's too low, the seat's 
too high, and the tires are too thin.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:53.250
Can you even ride this thing?

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:56.100
That's just how road bikes are.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:16:00.600
When you make a bike as light as possible 
and remove all excess so it'll go fast,

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.850
that's what it ends up looking like.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:05.370
That means you can easily 
go far on this bike, right?

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.880
I guess you could say that.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:09.190
Huh...

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:15.290
Oh, my!

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.640
Are you dressed like that 
so you can run faster, too?

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:20.450
That's not a swimsuit, is it?

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:23.670
Apparently, they're called racer pants.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:26.710
They have pads on the butt.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.430
I was told to wear these when I ride my bike.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.380
Oh, sorry. I broke it.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.090
What?

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.260
I think I bent it.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:37.300
Oh, that's okay. That's the gear shifter.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:40.020
Really? That's how it works, huh?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.570
Don't worry about shifting gears.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:47.460
Start by focusing on starting and stopping.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:48.670
Got it.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:49.720
There!

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:54.950
It has an unusual shape, 
but it's still a bicycle.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.950
This is easy.

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:03.030
Not bad for a beginner.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.210
Right?

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:08.630
I'm not particularly athletic,
but I can do what I've been taught.

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:13.920
They're here.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.190
Huh? That person...

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:19.080
Well? Have you heard anything?

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.360
Yeah, they just found her.

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:23.140
They're on their way here.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:25.700
Really? Oh, good.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:29.050
Hiromi, over here!

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:30.320
Tomo-chan!

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:34.100
Shiki-sensei! I finally found you.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:36.360
Just how far did you go?

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.290
I'm just glad you're all right.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:41.370
I have these people to thank for that.

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:46.210
Th-They seem kind of intense.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.790
But they're nice people.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:51.550
The walnut jam rolls are waiting for you.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.350
Head into the shop.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:58.160
Sensei, is this...

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:02.180
That's right. My little sister
 Nagisa and her shop.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.260
Who are you girls?

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:06.510
Higa Natsumi-san and Kamikura Fuyune-san.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:10.000
They're new customers 
at Bakery Flat, I think.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.650
And this is...

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.860
Shiki-sensei, right?

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.820
Oh, do you know me?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.280
Which means...

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:21.640
I'm a student in Minami 
Kamakura High Class 1-D.

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:23.350
I'm in Class C.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.650
Natsumi, you're a student 
at Minami Kamakura, too?

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:27.710
You, too?

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.620
That makes us classmates.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:33.130
Tomo-chan and I are in Class B.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:38.480
So we happen to have four 
new students here, huh?

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.760
What should we do now?

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:41.890
What?

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:44.640
Weren't you in the middle of 
showing us around Kamakura?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:47.060
Why don't we all keep riding together?

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.460
All of us?

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.310
I don't have a bicycle.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:51.740
Nagisa?

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:55.590
Yeah, yeah. You want me to 
go get the spare bike, right?

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.530
Higa-san, you'll come, too, won't you?

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.950
Sure, but where are we going?

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.810
Where should we go?

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.410
Well...

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:07.620
How about Enoshima?

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:11.030
Wow, Enoshima? I'm in!

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:12.430
It's decided, then.

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.980
<i>This is a strange feeling.</i>

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:29.650
<i>I can't believe I'm riding 
with people I just met.</i>

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.980
<i>Is this all because of bicycles?</i>

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:38.820
<i>Maybe bicycles are more 
amazing than I realized.</i>

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.660
<b>Benten</b>

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:19.090
I met a strange girl today.

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:23.240
Really? I met an interesting girl, too.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:25.490
Really? You, too?

00:21:25.490 --> 00:21:26.590
I'm home.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:28.780
Welcome home, Sis.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.820
Was it cold out?

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:34.980
Yeah. We'll have to keep the 
kotatsu out for a while longer.

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:40.160
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.250
<i>A-O-P: The first cycling club.</i>

