<b>Proper posture</b>

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:48.490
<i>In this segment, we bring you must-see 
information for newbies to road bikes with</i>

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:53.850
<b>Fukuo Yui</b>

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:53.850
<b>Hirose Yuki</b>

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:50.690
<i>A-O-P's Hirose Yuki...</i>

00:21:50.690 --> 00:21:52.900
<i>And Fukuo Yui.</i>

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:58.760
<i>Unlike normal bikes, road bikes are 
broken up by small differences in size.</i>

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:02.680
<i>"I don't know which one's right for me!"</i>

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:05.590
<i>"The differences are so small,
I can't choose."</i>

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:09.460
<i>"What should we do?"</i>

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:12.100
Gloom

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:12.100
<i>In order to make sure that 
doesn't happen to you,</i>

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:17.100
<b>Choosing a Bike 2: Choosing Based on Size</b>

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:15.250
<i>we'll learn how to choose the right size.</i>

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:21.770
How do you choose the right 
size road bike for yourself?

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:26.040
There are a few ways to decide 
which size is right for you,

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:29.280
<b>Y's Road Ochanomizu
Manager Yamada Yunosuke-san</b>

00:22:26.040 --> 00:22:27.420
so I thought we could try them out today.

00:22:27.420 --> 00:22:29.290
Yes, please.

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:34.780
Could you start by straddling this section,
which is known as the top tube?

00:22:34.780 --> 00:22:35.890
Okay.

00:22:35.890 --> 00:22:39.870
That's it. When you get on and off a bike, 
you'll always end up in this position,

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:44.430
so choosing a size that allows you 
to straddle the top tube is one way

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:47.510
<b>Choosing the Right Size 1
Height that allows you to easily straddle the top tube</b>

00:22:44.430 --> 00:22:46.860
to pick the right size.

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:51.160
The second way is the ability 
to raise the saddle to a height

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:55.390
<b>Choosing the Right Size 2
Saddle position that allows for effective pedaling</b>

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:55.390
where you're able to 
effectively turn the pedals.

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:58.200
Stop pedaling when your right 
foot reaches the lowest point.

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:02.570
The bottom of your foot and 
the ground are parallel.

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:06.890
Your knee should be bent 
about 160 to 170 degrees.

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:12.320
<b>Knee bent at 160 to 170 degrees</b>

00:23:06.890 --> 00:23:12.320
If this feels uncomfortable, 
then you'll lose power as you pedal.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.990
So you can't effectively use your power.

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:17.970
To pedal effectively, you should lower the saddle.

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:17.970
I see.

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:29.010
<b>People Who Want to Go Fast</b>

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:29.010
<b>People Who Want to Go Far</b>

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:29.010
<b>Choosing the Right Size 3
Handlebars let you find the right posture for your goals</b>

00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:21.870
<i>Furthermore, cyclists wanting 
to go fast should lean forward.</i>

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:25.010
<i>Cyclists wanting to go 
far should sit upright.</i>

00:23:25.010 --> 00:23:27.960
<i>Choose the right handlebar 
position based on your goals.</i>

